 ## Operating characteristics
-* **Time Complexity:** Dominated by iterating over all grid cells and solving the least-squares system for surface-intersecting cells. The cell iteration is $O(grid\_size^3)$. The least-squares solve is $O(N)$ per cell, where $N$ is the number of intersection points, which is typically small [S1, unofficial].
-* **Memory Complexity:** $O(grid\_size^3)$ for storing the ground truth arrays. The HDF5 file size scales linearly with the number of grid resolutions and objects [S1, unofficial].
-* **Strengths:** Provides explicit geometric ground truth (plane parameters) that is robust for training CNNs to predict Marching Cubes configurations. Handles multi-resolution LODs efficiently [S1, unofficial].
-* **Limitations:** Relies on external executables for SDF and intersection generation. The regularization and boundary adjustment loop can be computationally expensive if many cells have ill-conditioned intersection sets [S1, unofficial].
